<title>BELGIUM: EU REJECTS TEXTILE AID, BUT OPEN TO TALKS.</title>
<headline>EU REJECTS TEXTILE AID, BUT OPEN TO TALKS.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it had banned a French state aid scheme targeted at the textiles and clothing industries, but said it was open to discussions about a plan that would apply more widely.</p>
<p>EU Competition Commissioner Karel Van Miert has invited French authorities to discuss ways of broadening or widening the system, for example to cover all sectors that are heavily dependent on manual labour, it said in a statement.</p>
</text>
